d server C to stay reachable after its removal, since its acknowledgement is what the stale majority counted; if it we\n2 One could argue the snapshot in the durable-state case is only as good as the state the node tracks, and that a caller should not snapshot a node whose configur\n3 The flag-off restart's failure to lead could be attributed to the 1500ms observation window rather than to the empty configuration. The counter is the source gu\n4 The harness assigns roles deliberately (A restarts, B is partitioned, leadership is moved with the library's transfer) and it takes the snapshot explicitly rath\n5 The first execution of the multi-node experiment failed in the harness before any comparison (receipt 4ed46b198c8d41618cc855df0a63d469) and is retained as a har\n\nsingle-voter mentions: []\nargued mentions: []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ncfg=json.load(open('update18.json'))['interpretations'][0]\ncfg=json.loads(json.dumps(cfg))\ncfg['executions']['4178d9d5c479470cafb7ebd7951a9332']=[15,16,17,18]\n\n# strengthen the observation-window counterevidence\nold_win=\\\"The flag-off restart's failure to lead could be attributed to the 1500ms observation window rather than to the empty configuration. The counter is the source guard that refuses elections while configurations.latestIndex is zero (raft.go:225-241), together with the control on the same prefix shape that elected itself in 19 polls of the harness's 5ms interval, about 95ms (receipt 9a373c13725a42aa9f48f59c0f2f2f1c, event 6 records polls 19 and leader_observed true); 1500ms is 30 election timeouts.\\\"\nnew_win=\\\"The flag-off restart's failure to lead could be attributed to the 1500ms observation window rather than to the empty configuration. The counter is the source guard that refuses elections while configurations.latestIndex is zero (raft.go:225-241) plus two controls inside the same window: the single-voter control elected itself in 19 polls of the harness's 5ms interval (receipt 9a373c13725a42aa9f48f59c0f2f2f1c, event 6), and in the authority case the node that recovered its configuration was a candidate in 254 of 266 samples while the node with the empty configuration showed zero candidate samples (receipt 4178d9d5c479470cafb7ebd7951a9332, events 16 and 18).\\\"\nassert old_win in cfg['counterevidence']\ncfg['counterevidence']=[new_win if c==old_win else c for c in cfg['counterevidence']]\ncfg['counterevidence'].append(\\\"The authority case removes the other voters by shutting them down, so it shows that the defective node never attempts candidacy; it does not show an outage that a correct recovery would have prevented, because the recovered three-voter configuration also lacks a quorum with one voter left. What the receipt adds is the capability difference, not a counterfactual outage.\\\")\n\n# add the authority paragraph to the rationale\nanchor=\\\"Second consequence, durable: receipt c477da09810f4842ba55130320e2a6b5\\\"\nauth=(\\\"Authority attempt. Receipt 4178d9d5c479470cafb7ebd7951a9332 builds a three-voter group, commits three commands so the staged commit \\\"\n \\\"index is non-zero, restarts A over its own stores and reads its tracked configuration: with the replay enabled A tracks no configuration at \\\"\n \\\"all (event 15: latest_config_index 0, no members, staged commit index 4), and in 266 samples over 1500ms of hearing no leader with the other \\\"\n \\\"voters shut down it was a follower in every sample and never a candidate (event 16, comparison violated); with the replay disabled the same \\\"\n \\\"node and the same log recover the three-voter configuration (event 17: latest_config_index 1, three members) and the node was a candidate in \\\"\n \\\"254 of 266 samples, ending in state Candidate (event 18, comparison holds). A node whose tracked configuration is empty therefore does not \\\"\n \\\"merely fail to win an election: it never attempts to acquire authority, so it cannot be the source of a new leader even when the surviving \\\"\n \\\"members could form a quorum with it. \\\")\nassert anchor in cfg['rationale']\ncfg['rationale']=cfg['rationale'].replace(anchor, auth+anchor)\ncfg['rationale']=(\\\"Extension note: this successor adds receipt 4178d9d5c479470cafb7ebd7951a9332, which observes in a three-voter group that a node recovering \\\"\n \\\"without a configuration never attempts candidacy while the same node and log with the replay disabled do; the sources, the three earlier executions, the \\\"\n \\\"knowledge uses, the conclusion and the remaining counterevidence are otherwise unchanged, and the counter about the observation window is strengthened \\\"\n \\\"with the new control's sample counts. \\\")+cfg['rationale']\ncfg['joint_history']=cfg['joint_history'].replace(\\\"All three receipts are executions\\\",\\\"All four receipts are executions\\\")\ncfg['joint_history']+=\\\" Receipt 4178d9d5c479470cafb7ebd7951a9332 uses the same three-voter construction as receipt 79a9cc34b3ce42e197c384775efecc3a and reports the same tracked-configuration operands (latest index, voter count, member ids) after a replay-enabled restart, with the replay-disabled restart of the same node and log as its control.\\\"\nout={\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Extends the configuration-recovery account with receipt 4178d9d5c479470cafb7ebd7951a9332 (a voter that recovers no configuration never attempts candidacy) and strengthens the observation-window counter with that receipt's control samples.\\\",\n     \\\"interpretations\\\":[cfg]}\njson.dump(out,open('update23.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('execs',list(cfg['executions'].keys()),'ce',len(cfg['counterevidence']),'lim',len(cfg['limitations']))\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update23.json 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"\nimport sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint('valid',d['valid'],'no_change',d.get('no_change'))\nfor x in d.get('diagnostics',[])[:6]: print(x['paths'],x['message'])\nprint([(e['object'],e['action']) for e in d.get('effects',[])])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
